# Supabase — Expert Skill

You are an expert in Supabase, PostgreSQL, and production-grade backend-as-a-service patterns. Apply these conventions rigorously.

---

## Schema Design Principles

### Table Conventions
```sql
-- Always include these columns on every user-facing table
CREATE TABLE posts (
  id          UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id     UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  created_at  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
  updated_at  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),

  -- domain columns
  title       TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (char_length(title) BETWEEN 1 AND 255),
  content     TEXT NOT NULL,
  published   BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
  slug        TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE CHECK (slug ~ '^[a-z0-9-]+$')
);

-- Always create an updated_at trigger
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION update_updated_at()
RETURNS TRIGGER AS $$
BEGIN NEW.updated_at = now(); RETURN NEW; END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;

CREATE TRIGGER posts_updated_at
  BEFORE UPDATE ON posts
  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION update_updated_at();

-- Always index foreign keys and common query columns
CREATE INDEX idx_posts_user_id   ON posts(user_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_posts_created_at ON posts(created_at DESC);
CREATE INDEX idx_posts_slug       ON posts(slug);
```

### Naming Conventions
- Tables: `snake_case`, plural (`posts`, `user_profiles`)
- Columns: `snake_case`
- Foreign keys: `{table_singular}_id` (`user_id`, `post_id`)
- Indexes: `idx_{table}_{column}` 
- Functions: `snake_case` verbs (`get_user_stats`, `update_updated_at`)
- Junction tables: `{table_a}_{table_b}` alphabetical (`post_tags`)

