## Migration Workflow

```bash
# Start local Supabase (Docker required)
supabase start

# Create a new migration
supabase migration new add_posts_table

# Apply pending migrations locally
supabase db push

# Diff your local schema changes into a migration file
supabase db diff -f my_changes

# Reset local DB and replay all migrations from scratch
supabase db reset

# Pull remote schema to local
supabase db pull

# Push migrations to production
supabase db push --linked
```

- **Never** hand-edit the remote DB directly — always use migrations
- Commit migration files to git — they are the source of truth
- Run `supabase gen types typescript` after every migration

### Free-Tier Keep-Alive
Supabase free-tier projects pause after 1 week of inactivity:
```typescript
// workers/supabase-keepalive.ts — run via PM2, ping every 4 days
import { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js';

const supabase = createClient(process.env.SUPABASE_URL!, process.env.SUPABASE_ANON_KEY!);

async function ping() {
  const { error } = await supabase.from('_keepalive').select('id').limit(1).maybeSingle();
  console.log(error ? `[keepalive] error: ${error.message}` : '[keepalive] ok');
}

setInterval(ping, 4 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000); // every 4 days
ping(); // immediate on startup
```

